---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { methods, statusFields } from "../../data/api";
const categories = Array.from(new Set(methods.map(method => method.category)));
const cliExamples = "lunadashctl status\nlunadashctl workspace 1\nlunadashctl appearance '{\"gap\":16,\"animations\":true}'\nlunadashctl quit confirm";
const wireRequest = "{\"method\":\"appearance\",\"value\":\"{\\\"gap\\\":16}\"}\n";
const directSocket = "import json, os, socket\n\npath = os.environ.get(\"LUNADASH_CONTROL\") or os.environ.get(\"LUDASH_CONTROL\")\nif not path:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"LUNADASH_CONTROL is not set\")\n\nrequest = {\"method\": \"appearance\", \"value\": json.dumps({\"gap\": 16})}\nwith socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX) as client:\n    client.settimeout(3)\n    client.connect(path)\n    client.sendall(json.dumps(request).encode() + b\"\\n\")\n    data = b\"\"\n    while b\"\\n\" not in data:\n        chunk = client.recv(65536)\n        if not chunk or len(data) + len(chunk) > 1024 * 1024:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Invalid LunaDash response\")\n        data += chunk\n\nresponse = json.loads(data.split(b\"\\n\", 1)[0])\nif \"error\" in response:\n    raise RuntimeError(response[\"error\"])\nprint(json.dumps(response, indent=2))";
const networkExamples = "lunadashctl network '{\"action\":\"wifi-scan\"}'\nlunadashctl network '{\"action\":\"wifi-connect\",\"ssid\":\"Lab WiFi\",\"password\":\"...\"}'\nlunadashctl network '{\"action\":\"networking-enable\",\"enabled\":true}'\nlunadashctl network '{\"action\":\"connection-ipv4-manual\",\"name\":\"Lab\",\"address\":\"192.0.2.20/24\",\"gateway\":\"192.0.2.1\",\"dns\":\"1.1.1.1\"}'";
const targetIds = "builtin:<extension-target>\nplugin:<package-id>:<extension-target>\nmodule:<module-id>:<section>\nlayout:<active-window-template>";
const settingsPatch = "# Read descriptors\nlunadashctl settings-describe\n\n# Send the selected target's exact revision with a partial change\nlunadashctl settings-update '{\"target\":\"plugin:org.example.motion:window-animation\",\"revision\":\"<64-hex-sha256>\",\"changes\":{\"duration\":280}}'";
const nativeAbi = "#include <stddef.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n\n#define LUDASH_PLUGIN_API_VERSION 2u\n\ntypedef struct ludash_plugin_api {\n    uint32_t struct_size;\n    uint32_t api_version;\n    const char *metadata_json;\n    int (*process)(const char *request, char *response, size_t capacity);\n} ludash_plugin_api;\n\nint ludash_plugin_process(const char *request, char *response, size_t capacity);\nconst ludash_plugin_api *ludash_plugin_entry_v2(void);\nint ludash_plugin_write_json(const char *json, char *response, size_t capacity);";
const nativeEnvelope = "{\n  \"target\":\"window-animation\",\n  \"mode\":\"replace\",\n  \"context\":{},\n  \"builtin\":{\"duration\":220,\"enterOffset\":12,\"focusOpacity\":0.82,\"exitScale\":0.9,\"easing\":\"outCubic\"},\n  \"current\":{},\n  \"settings\":{\"duration\":280}\n}";
---
<DocsLayout title="Every way to talk to LunaDash." section="api" summary="LunaDash exposes one owner-only Unix control socket, a versioned Settings API and Plugin SDK 2's synchronous C ABI; the shell reaches it through SlintLu. This page documents the contracts implemented by the current source tree.">
  <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#wire">Wire protocol</a><a href="#status">Status</a><a href="#methods">Methods</a><a href="#settings-api">Settings API</a><a href="#native">Native ABI</a></nav>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>This is a local session API, not HTTP.</strong> LunaDash listens on a Unix socket that only your user can open. The website documents the API; it cannot control a running desktop.</p></div>

  <h2 id="wire">Wire protocol and ludashctl</h2>
  <p>Processes launched by LunaDash inherit <code>LUNADASH_CONTROL</code>. The client still accepts the historical <code>LUDASH_CONTROL</code>, then searches the runtime directory for one unambiguous <code>*-control</code> socket. Prefer <code>LUNADASH_CONTROL</code> in new code.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={cliExamples} />
  <p>The CLI sends one compact UTF-8 JSON object followed by a newline. <code>method</code> and <code>value</code> are strings, so structured payloads are JSON encoded inside <code>value</code>. The compositor accepts at most 65,536 request bytes, applies a three-second server timeout and returns one compact JSON object plus a newline.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="WIRE REQUEST" code={wireRequest} />
  <p>Invalid JSON returns <code>{'{"error":"Invalid request"}'}</code>. An unsupported method/value returns <code>{'{"error":"Invalid command or value"}'}</code>. <code>lunadashctl</code> waits up to 1.5 seconds per socket read and refuses responses larger than 1 MiB.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="DIRECT SOCKET / PYTHON" code={directSocket} />

  <h2 id="status">Status is the discovery API</h2>
  <p>Use <code>status</code> to discover client ids, display modes, connection names, plugin ids, available power/session actions and layout actions instead of hard-coding host-specific values.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody>{statusFields.map(field => <tr><td class="api-method">{field.name}</td><td><code>{field.type}</code></td><td>{field.purpose}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Each ordinary <code>status.clients[]</code> entry includes a positive session-local id, title, app id, icon, desktop id, X11 flag, workspace, geometry, focus/minimize/maximize/fullscreen/mapped flags and buffer/content sizes. Do not persist these ids across compositor restarts.</p>

  <h2 id="methods">Every control method</h2>
  <p>The tables are aligned with <code>WaylandCompositor::control()</code> on the dev branch. Examples use the CLI form; direct socket clients send the same method/value pair.</p>
  {categories.map(category => (
    <section>
      <h3>{category}</h3>
      <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        {methods.filter(method => method.category === category).map(method => <tr><td class="api-method">{method.name}</td><td>{method.value}</td><td>{method.behavior}</td><td><code>{method.example}</code></td></tr>)}
      </tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h3>Network action payloads</h3>
  <p><code>network</code> accepts structured operations, never arbitrary <code>nmcli</code> text. Actions are <code>bluetooth-scan</code>, <code>network-reset</code>, <code>connection-reconnect</code>, <code>wifi-scan</code>, <code>wifi-connect</code>, <code>connection-up/down/delete</code>, <code>device-connect/disconnect</code>, <code>networking-enable</code>, <code>wifi-enable</code>, <code>connection-autoconnect</code>, <code>connection-ipv4-auto/manual</code>, <code>connection-ipv6-auto/disabled</code> and <code>connection-route-metric</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="NETWORK EXAMPLES" code={networkExamples} />

  <h3>Shortcut ids</h3>
  <p>Known actions are <code>focusLeft/Right/Up/Down</code>, <code>groupLeft/Right</code>, <code>reorderLeft/Right</code>, <code>expelWindow</code>, <code>centerColumn</code>, <code>widenColumn</code>, <code>narrowColumn</code>, <code>maximizeWindow</code>, <code>toggleFullscreen</code>, <code>toggleTilingMode</code>, <code>closeWindow</code>, <code>minimizeWindow</code>, <code>launchTerminal</code>, <code>launchFiles</code>, <code>launchLauncher</code>, <code>launchOrbit</code>, <code>chooseWallpaper</code>, <code>randomWallpaper</code>, <code>toggleEyeCare</code>, <code>toggleScratchpad</code>, <code>openControlCenter</code>, <code>openClipboard</code>, <code>openPowerMenu</code>, <code>screenshot</code>, plus <code>workspace1..10</code> and <code>moveToWorkspace1..10</code>. Values are <code>Meta</code>/<code>Alt</code>/<code>Ctrl</code>/<code>Shift</code> combinations such as <code>Meta+Shift+Space</code>, or <code>Disabled</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="settings-api">Settings API version 1</h2>
  <p><code>settings-describe</code> returns descriptors with <code>id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>category</code>, normalized <code>schema</code>, current <code>values</code> and a SHA-256 <code>revision</code>. The revision hashes schema plus values for optimistic concurrency.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="TARGET ID FORMS" code={targetIds} />
  <CodeBlock label="PATCH FLOW" code={settingsPatch} />
  <p>If another editor changed the target, the patch fails with <code>Settings changed. Reload before applying this edit.</code>. Schemas can describe boolean, string, integer, number and bounded enum-array fields. Plugin schemas intentionally allow only toggle, select, number and slider controls.</p>

  <h2 id="native">Native Plugin SDK 2 ABI</h2>
  <p>Native effects do not receive wlroots pointers. Hooks run synchronously on the compositor thread over UTF-8 JSON; do not block, retain host pointers, run nested event loops or create lifetime-escaping callbacks/background work.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="ABI" code={nativeAbi} />
  <p>The SDK generates <code>ludash_plugin_entry_v2</code>, embeds the built manifest and produces the receipt. The loader checks struct size, API version 2, process pointer and equality between embedded and installed metadata.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="REQUEST ENVELOPE" code={nativeEnvelope} />
  <p><code>builtin</code> is always available. Replacement hooks get empty <code>current</code>; augment hooks receive the previous valid result. Return a complete JSON object and its byte length excluding NUL, or a negative value. The response buffer is 262,145 bytes. Invalid/oversized output quarantines the instance and preserves the built-in/previous result.</p>
  <p>The native targets are <code>window-animation</code>, <code>shell-animation</code>, <code>window-rules</code> and <code>window-layout</code>; see <a href="../plugins/">Compositor plugins</a>.</p>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Trust boundary:</strong> native effects run inside the compositor without a sandbox.</p></div>
</DocsLayout>
